// A SCHEDULED run must complete the period it was dispatched for.
//
// `window_start` reaches us inside a signed token, so the agent cannot invent
// one — but it CAN steer which period gets minted, because `get_content`
// Behavior mode honours `since`/`until` and mints the token for that range
// instead of the dispatched window. Nothing downstream noticed: `findCanvasHead`
// matches the token's period exactly, finds the old root, and supersedes it, so
// the run reports success while the window never advances.
//
// That is not hypothetical. Behavior 71 ran hourly for a full day dispatched
// `2026-07-30T23:59:59.999Z` and completing `2026-07-30T00:00:00.000Z` — 13
// scheduled runs, every one `completed`. Across the six Behaviors with
// scheduled completions, period mismatch correlates perfectly with an
// end-of-day (`toEndOfDay`) window end, which is the `since`/`until` signature:
// the one Behavior whose periods match uses period-aligned ends on all 22 of
// its windows.
//
// Rejected rather than silently retargeted, and the message names the fix so
// the agent can recover inside the same turn (same contract as the invalid
// -token path above). Writing the digest into the wrong period is worse than
// not writing it: it looks like output, so nothing ever surfaces the failure.
//
// Only scheduled runs. A manual or event run legitimately carries whatever
// period its caller chose.
if (
  dispatchSource === 'scheduled' &&
  dispatchedWindowStart != null &&
  new Date(dispatchedWindowStart).getTime() !== new Date(window_start).getTime()
) {
  throw new ToolUserError(
    `This run was dispatched for the period starting ${dispatchedWindowStart}, but the ` +
      `window_token covers ${window_start}. A scheduled Behavior must complete the period it ` +
      'was given. Re-read with get_content WITHOUT `since`/`until` — those override the ' +
      'dispatched window — and complete using the token from that response.'
  );
}

